                <pb facs="0875" n="787" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg787"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Count
                            Cassini.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-09-16"><hi rendition="#italic">September 16,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: Your telegram of yesterday
                    reached me in the evening. As I explained to Mr. Hansen, the request of my
                    telegram of the 14th for a decision between the alternatives in the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lena</hi> case was superseded by the formal application
                    of Captain Berlinsky and by my telegram to you of yesterday morning apprising
                    you of the decision to disarm. I am glad the incident has been so satisfactorily
                    closed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
